=== what rung 4 does not carry over from APL ===

SKIP  ⍺⍺ ⍵⍵ ∇∇  out of scope: a direct OPERATOR takes its operands as names, and a name in a template is a free Fortress identifier: rung 5 or 6
SKIP  f⍤0 and f⍤3  out of scope: only ⍤1 and ⍤2 have rules; the rank is a terminal of the grammar, not a value
SKIP  +/⍤1⊢m  out of scope: a REDUCTION is not a member of the glyph tables, so it cannot be an operand of ⍤; the dfn {+/⍵} is (X13)
SKIP  0 2 1⍉t  out of scope: every axis permutation but 1 0 2 is a contract violation (X30); monadic ⍉ on rank 3 has no rule at all
SKIP  a dfn's last statement  out of scope: a dfn whose body ends with a binding has no production, as at the top level (rung 2); the chapter's Ex 15 and Ex 16 get their bound name appended
SKIP  ⍵ in a nested dfn  out of scope: APL's own rule that ⍺ ⍵ are never inherited is free here: a nested dfn's ⍵ is its own because its call pushed its own frame (X23)
